# Review gates

Follow the risk levels in `AGENTS.md`.

## Design review

Before code, record blast radius and callers, duplication check, proposed interfaces, invariants, edge/failure/concurrency cases, migration/rollback impact, observability, and test plan. Split the ticket if these do not form one concern.

## Implementation review

Use a fresh reviewer that did not implement the change. Review UX, correctness, edge cases, performance, testing, architecture, consistency, accessibility, security, data integrity, API contracts, and operability. Verdicts are PASS, CHANGES_REQUIRED, or BLOCKED.

CHANGES_REQUIRED requires fixes followed by a complete new review. BLOCKED requires escalation, not a workaround. One independent implementation reviewer is the default at every risk level. Add a second reviewer only when the ticket defines a materially different charter that the first reviewer cannot adequately cover; shared interfaces or critical paths alone do not justify duplicate general reviews. Use a security-focused charter for auth, uploads, data access, secrets, or money movement.

No model or price tier is required. Use the least costly reviewer capable of the charter and escalate only for unresolved specialist risk or explicit user direction.

Every PASS must cite acceptance-criterion code paths, relevant test names, and actual quality-gate output. Unverified claims remain unverified.
